<title>FRANCE: French grain use in feed up 10 pct, July-March.</title>
<headline>French grain use in feed up 10 pct, July-March.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>French cereals office ONIC on Wednesday released the following breakdown of grain consumption for commercial animal feed in France this season.</p>
<p>The figures, in thousands of tonnes, are for the first nine months of the July/June season up to March 31.</p>
<p>			  Soft wheat Barley   Maize   Durum   Total</p>
<p> 1996/97 (Jul-Mar)    4,292.4   785.3  1,727.7   0.0   6,805.4</p>
<p> 1995/96 (Jul-Mar)    4,199.7   598.0  1,390.1   0.3   6,188.1</p>
<p> Percent change	    +2.2   +31.3    +24.3   ---     +10.0</p>
<p> 96/97 est. (Jul-Jun)   5,700   1,000    2,600     0     9,300</p>
<p> 95/96 (Jul-Jun)	5,583.7   867.3  1,916.5   0.3   8,367.8</p>
<p>ONIC also released the following data for non-grain feed imports between July and the end of February (thousand tonnes).</p>
<p>			   Manioc     Corn gluten	Total</p>
<p> 1996/97 (Jul-Feb)    75.7	   87.5	    452.2</p>
<p> 1995/96 (Jul-Feb)    54.4	  206.1	    575.9</p>
<p>--- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
</text>
